                         BackGround & Purpose
                         ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
I was sick and tired of having alot of different utils to do my bulletins
(Some of them had really bad design too), so i started coding this nice and
easy util. This tool will replace the most of your utils. It will create your:

Top Uploaders (In Bytes)
Top Uploaders (In Files)
Top Downloaders (In Bytes)
Top Downloaders (In Files)
Top Message Writers
Top Calls
Top Upload CPS
Top Download CPS


                   The syntax of Multitop (How to use)
                   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
                The SYNTAX for multitop is the following:

  MULTITOP <userdata> <outputfile> <mode> <# users> [<userkeys>]

     <userdata>   -  The FULL path to your USER.DATA file.
     <outputfile> -  The FULL path to outputfile. You may enter a STAR (*)
                     to send the output directly to screen.
     <mode>       -  7 different modes are availible for the moment. They are:

                     MODE (0) - Top Uploaders (Bytes)
                     MODE (1) - Top Downloaders (Bytes)
                     MODE (2) - Top Uploaders (Files)
                     MODE (3) - Top Downloaders (Files)
                     MODE (4) - Top Message Writers
                     MODE (5) - Top Calls
                     MODE (6) - Top Upload CPS
                     MODE (7) - Top Download CPS

     <# users>    -  How many users you want in the output. The output have
                     two colums, so if you enter 30 users, it will be 15
                     lines.

     [<userkeys>] -  The FULL path to your USER.KEYS file. This is ONLY needed
                     for MODE 6 & 7.

          Example >: MULTITOP BBS:USER.DATA BBS:BULL.TXT 0 30
                     - This would output the 30 top uploaders (bytes)
                       to BBS:Bull.txt.

                  >: MULTITOP BBS:USER.DATA * 6 30 BBS:USER.KEYS
                     - This would output the 30 top upload CPS
                       directly to screen.

                  >: MULTITOP BBS:USER.DATA BBS:BULL.TXT 5 50
                     - This would output the 50 top callers
                       to BBS:Bull.txt.


                        Use a Header/Tailer
                        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Multitop will always search for a headerfile/tailerfile ..

· S:Multitop.Header - for add before the output, and
· S:Multitop.Tailer - for add after the output.

If no headerfile is found, a clear-screen (CTRL-L) is added so it displays
quicker/nicer.

NOTE: When you are using a own headerfile, don't forget the clear-screen at
      the top!


